From 511ddff0a3a8cf637fb5e8fcfdf0c24190e8b819 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Til Kaiser <mail@tk154.de>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:53:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] wolfguard: add eBPF kfuncs for explicit peer traffic
 accounting

Traffic handled through the WolfGuard crypto kfuncs bypasses native peer
accounting. Add bpf_wolf_peer_update_rx_stats and
bpf_wolf_peer_update_tx_stats so XDP and TC programs can account for
accepted receive traffic and committed transmits explicitly.

Count the full data message, including the header, padding and AES-GCM
authentication tag, while excluding UDP and IP headers. Reject empty
keepalives and shorter messages without changing counters. Update only
peer bytes; device byte, packet, error and drop counters stay unchanged.
The accounting calls preserve their input references.

Convert peer byte counters to atomic64_t and update initialization, native
writers and netlink readers to preserve concurrent native/BPF increments.
Document the explicit accounting responsibilities, message-length contract
and unchanged device counters.
